  "service_contract_additions": {
    "x_authority_gate_schema": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] Executor must independently READ an attributable CHG and bound D007 release from authoritative services, verifying scope, target UUID, full tree, validity, state and non-Claude D009 outcome. Caller-supplied strings, local matching hashes, approved design-only CHGs and service catalogue status are not authority. Reject forged CHG-2027-999, expired/foreign permissions, wrong target, reused decision, stale state, D009 self-assurance, missing restore and runner identity. Existing C02 gate and installer are HELD after false-GO adversarial reproduction.",
    "x_deterministic_tech_requirements": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] Four gates: qualified complete Git source; ZIP-optional allowlisted staged SSH/rsync transfer with DESTINATION hashes; tested atomic one-writer Odoo module upgrade after verified consistent full restore; post-version, signed-in roles, browser 390 px, second-cycle, human acceptance. No live tree overlay; no fixed destination assumption. Recovery restores consistent DB, filestore, code trio after schema change.",
    "x_execution_input_contract": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] Bind exact Work Object/current state, expected return, Git commit, complete addon tree and per-file hashes, source dependencies and migration, target host/database UUID/container/mount, role and capability test receipts, approved CHG and D007 effect release, D009 independent assurance, consistent DB+filestore recovery pair, negative tests and acceptance actor. A file format/ZIP is optional, not a release identity.",
    "x_execution_outcome_schema": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] Return release_id, consumed Work Object/state/hash, source and target identities; each gate with actual evidence/missing controls; actor->capability direct-probe receipt (runtime, version, native mode, permission, controlled failure, expiry); chosen AI complement/independence; transfer hash readback; restore test; rehearsal; authority/D007; actual version/readback/UI/role/mobile checks; false HOLD/PROCEED; recovery and second-cycle result; human acceptance; exact one NEXT and replay state. Do not label untested gates PASSED.",
    "x_execution_profile_requirements": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] Service progression: source -> transfer -> rehearsal -> authority -> install -> accept/recover, each with exact immutable release ID and truthful FILED/TRANSFERRED/VERIFIED/REHEARSED/INSTALLED/ACCEPTED states. Preserve completed work and main path; two retries in same class -> qualified alternative or local HOLD. Run AI capability and composition challenge before choosing provider. Separate 316-row load as another release.",
    "x_observation_learning_contract": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] Record AI capability availability/delta, capability substitution impact, failed actor/route, no-ZIP recovery, duplicate/idle cycles, false admission, cross-context leak, tested rollback/restore, duration and cost, incident owner and original-failure retest. Qualify one subsequent comparable cycle before proposing durable service effectiveness. Do not treat preparation as Benefit or Asset.",
    "x_provider_fallback_policy": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] ZIP absence must not block directory/rsync transfer when qualified. Substitute only pretested transport/actor with equal identity, rights, source, evidence and negative tests. Never substitute W11 Odoo.sh for Hostinger. Missing provider means HOLD; never infer that a tool listing equals executable entitlement.",
    "x_return_acceptance_schema": "[HOSTINGER-V20-RELEASE-QUALIFICATION-CANDIDATE] Reject any service result with invalid source/target/state, claimed capability without an actual native probe, untested required AI, Claude-as-D009 reviewer, forged self-supplied authority, absent destination hash, inconsistent G2 restore, no release, mock tests called production, missing changed-condition acceptance, or unsupported installed version. Accept separate readiness versus installer execution versus observed Outcome; independent readback after effects."
